1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Client handoffs need evidence.
Briefstamp turns requirements into approved checks and a report clients can read.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Start with six requirements.
This hosted walkthrough uses a synthetic website and clearly labelled template checks.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Approval comes before execution.
Review the plan, approve the checks, then run the browser audit.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
A real browser. Observed outcomes.
5 passed · 0 failed · 1 unverified. A subjective requirement still needs human judgment.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Change the sample. Keep the assertions.
Selecting the broken condition resets approvals. Review and approve again before running.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:37,000
The broken website fails three checks.
2 passed · 3 failed · 1 unverified. Missing evidence never becomes a pass.

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:44,000
See what the browser actually found.
The failed heading stays linked to its requirement and captured screenshot.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Restore the sample. Approve again.
Same assertions. The operator restores the synthetic condition; this is not automatic repair.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Three recoveries, checked by Chromium.
5 passed · 0 failed · 1 unverified. The subjective requirement remains unresolved.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Compare the same checks across runs.
3 recovered · 2 still passing · 1 unknown. Changed or manual checks cannot prove a fix.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Send the site. Show the proof.
Download a portable delivery report with observed results and screenshot evidence.
